WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.350
Neuroformer is a multimodal,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:06.416
multitask generative pretrained transformer for
brain data,

00:00:06.496 --> 00:00:08.207
built at UC Santa Barbara.

00:00:08.287 --> 00:00:14.479
It reframes cellular-resolution spike analysis as
autoregressive spatiotemporal generation,

00:00:14.559 --> 00:00:18.682
borrowing the recipe behind large language and
vision models.

00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:24.540
Trained self-supervised, it recovers circuit
connectivity and decodes mouse behavior.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:29.685
Modern neuroscience records thousands of neurons at
cellular resolution,

00:00:29.765 --> 00:00:32.243
alongside visual stimuli and behavior.

00:00:32.323 --> 00:00:35.473
These datasets are large, multimodal, and messy,

00:00:35.553 --> 00:00:40.386
yet the field's traditional statistical tools were
built for far smaller,

00:00:40.466 --> 00:00:44.760
single-modality recordings, leaving a widening
data-analysis gap.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.549
Large pretrained models in vision and language
point a way forward: they learn general

00:00:50.629 --> 00:00:53.485
representations self-supervised from raw data,

00:00:53.565 --> 00:00:55.719
then transfer with little labeling.

00:00:55.799 --> 00:01:01.655
The authors ask whether reframing spike analysis as
generative prediction can likewise scale,

00:01:01.735 --> 00:01:04.910
fuse modalities, and transfer to behavior decoding.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:07.957
Neuroformer makes four contributions.

00:01:08.037 --> 00:01:13.303
It reframes spike analysis as self-supervised
autoregressive generation,

00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:14.640
needing no labels.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.580
Its cross-attention scales linearly with feature
size and fuses many modalities.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.629
On simulated data, its attention maps recover
directed connectivity,

00:01:25.709 --> 00:01:28.673
including hub neurons correlation misses.

00:01:28.753 --> 00:01:32.980
Pretrained, it decodes behavior with few-shot fine-tuning.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.246
Neuroformer treats each spike as a token,

00:01:36.326 --> 00:01:39.717
splitting activity into Current and Past States.

00:01:39.797 --> 00:01:43.551
Video becomes patches via a 3D-convolutional encoder;

00:01:43.631 --> 00:01:45.938
behavior forms a separate stream.

00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:50.856
A contrastive module aligns neural, visual, and
behavioral features.

00:01:50.936 --> 00:01:55.703
Cross-attention fuses the Current State with larger
feature arrays,

00:01:55.783 --> 00:01:59.174
cutting attention cost from quadratic to linear.

00:01:59.254 --> 00:02:04.310
A causally masked decoder predicts which neuron
fires and its time bin.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:08.083
Validation spans two levels.

00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:11.556
First,

00:02:11.636 --> 00:02:15.029
a simulated spiking network with three hub neurons
gives a ground-truth connectivity matrix.

00:02:15.109 --> 00:02:18.501
Second,

00:02:18.581 --> 00:02:21.974
two-photon calcium imaging of mouse visual cortex
records 386 neurons across V1 and AL

00:02:22.054 --> 00:02:25.447
viewing gratings and natural videos,

00:02:25.527 --> 00:02:28.920
plus a virtual-navigation dataset pairing activity
with running speed.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.097
On the simulated network,

00:02:31.177 --> 00:02:37.477
Neuroformer's attention reveals directed
connectivity and identifies the hub neurons,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:41.831
which plain correlation misses for lack of directionality.

00:02:41.911 --> 00:02:47.161
On real cortex, it reproduces responses to gratings
and natural videos,

00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:52.490
with population predictions significantly beating a
GLM, p around 0.02.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:57.970
Fine-tuned to decode running, it reaches Pearson
correlations up to 0.97.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:03.413
An ablation removes components one at a time: the
Current State, Past State,

00:03:03.493 --> 00:03:05.443
video stream, behavior stream,

00:03:05.523 --> 00:03:09.706
and contrastive objective each add measurable
predictive power.

00:03:09.786 --> 00:03:11.263
Two findings stand out.

00:03:11.343 --> 00:03:15.932
Jointly training on neural responses and behavior
beats either alone,

00:03:16.012 --> 00:03:20.060
and the contrastive objective helps most when data
is scarce.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:26.946
For behavior prediction, Neuroformer reaches
Pearson correlation up to 0.97,

00:03:27.026 --> 00:03:29.372
versus about 0.73 for Lasso.

00:03:29.452 --> 00:03:36.478
Few-shot, a model pretrained and fine-tuned on just
1% of behavior data hits 0.51,

00:03:36.558 --> 00:03:42.197
beating a non-pretrained model given 10%, which
reaches only 0.33.

00:03:42.277 --> 00:03:47.310
Its largest models scale to roughly 100 million
parameters.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:54.081
The takeaway: the pretraining paradigm that
reshaped vision and language can also work for the brain.

00:03:54.161 --> 00:03:57.669
Treating spikes as autoregressive multimodal generation,

00:03:57.749 --> 00:04:04.972
one self-supervised transformer recovers a
circuit's directed connectivity and decodes behavior from few examples,

00:04:05.052 --> 00:04:08.560
pointing toward scalable neuroscience foundation models.
